	•	Section 2 Comments/Quotes: The paper states, “We identified 58 patients meeting criteria.” Baseline characteristics show mean age 35.8 years, and 65.5% male, implying 34.5% female. Race was reported as 91.4% White, 3.4% Black, and 5.2% Asian. Table 1 also includes multiple comorbidities such as hypertension, diabetes, pulmonary hypertension, portal hypertension, chronic renal insufficiency, and tobacco history.

