	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The Methods describe “a retrospective chart review” and state that “a machine learning decision tree model was used to evaluate multiple clinical parameters correlating with 1- and 10-year survival.” Input data were clinical, hemodynamic, laboratory, and CPET variables from chart review. The model was “verified… using K-fold cross validation.” The variables entered into multivariate analysis were those previously significant on univariate analysis, which is best categorized as manual/clinical feature selection. No hyperparameter tuning or explainability method was reported.

