	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The paper evaluates both 1-year and 10-year survival. Figure 1 and the text report clinically interpretable decision rules rather than AUC-style performance. For 1-year outcomes, transplanted patients with SVP <14 mmHg had 100% survival, and non-transplanted patients with PCWP <15 mmHg had 100% survival. For 10-year outcomes, all waitlisted/declined patients with PCWP ≥17 mmHg died, and all transplanted/deferred patients with SVP <10 mmHg were alive. Kaplan–Meier curves in Figure 2 show 1-year survival of 100% for deferred, 85.7% for transplanted, 42.1% for waitlisted, and 54.5% for declined patients. No AUC, accuracy, sensitivity, specificity, PPV, NPV, F1-score, calibration, or DCA were reported.

